  "title": "tribus Claudia",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/tribus"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The <em>tribus Claudia </em>was organized ca. 504 B.C. by Attius Clausus (also know more commonly as Appius Claudius). The tribal territory lay north of the Anio river, between Fidenae and Ficulea. The <em>tribus Claudia </em>adjoined the <em>tribus Clustumina.</em></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The tribus Claudia was the twenty-first rural tribe.",
